From 0d697655f358602f82cd67bc5396af0e56e4ace1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:56:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08/13] Round 8: Run a worker on the calling thread and cap
 threads at the CPUs

Batch dispatch now treats workers as an upper bound: it runs at most
min(workers, candidates, available_parallelism) threads, one of them
the calling thread, and caches the CPU count for the process. On this
2-vCPU host a four-worker request starts one extra thread instead of
four. Record order and results are unchanged.

Workload: parallel (96 full records, four requested workers), full API.
Official 11-sample run: 0.604 ms -> 0.514 ms, 1.18x (paired 1.11x).
41-sample confirmation: 0.626 ms -> 0.470 ms, paired 1.26x.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
